\label{sec:scope}

SICA as evaluated here uses \emph{same-model self-extraction}: the same LLM generates traces and extracts constraints. This design isolates whether a model's own reasoning can be usefully formalized for aggregation. Methods that use trained extractors, external provers, or multi-model ensembles fall outside the scope of this evaluation. We test nine remediation strategies spanning prompt, architecture, and solver dimensions (\S\ref{sec:interventions}), including Z3 Feedback Refinement (Appendix~\ref{app:z3-pseudocode}), a closed-loop paradigm \citep{kambhampati2024position} where the solver feeds UNSAT cores back to the extractor.

